---
title: Rice Cooker Beef Bowl
servings: 2
course: dinner
cuisine: Korean
tags: one-pan, make-ahead, beef, rice
source: https://www.youtube.com/@i.amneverfull
prep time: 5m
cook time: 25m
---

-- from the pinned comment on the video

In a #bowl{}, marinate @beef steak{170%g}(thinly sliced) with @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @garlic clove{2}(minced), @brown sugar{1%tbsp} and @sesame oil{1%tsp}. Let it sit for ~{15%minutes}.

Wash @long grain rice{200%g} thoroughly, then put it in the #rice cooker{} with @water{300%ml}. Layer the marinated beef on top without stirring it in.

Cook on the normal rice cooker setting until done, about ~{25%minutes}.

Scoop the rice into a #bowl{} and top with the beef. Garnish with @?sesame seed{1%tsp} and @?spring onion{2}(sliced).
